  "id": "sapirwhorf-hypothesis",
  "term": "Sapir–Whorf hypothesis",
  "definition": "The Sapir–Whorf hypothesis is the idea that the structure of language habitually shapes how people think. In this source, it is used in a weakened form that treats linguistic patterns as influencing cognition without making language an absolute limit on thought.",
